{"name":"Silver Sweetpea","hex":"#c4c9e2","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"silver","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A lustrous, white, metallic element, atomic number 47, atomic weight 107.87, symbol Ag.","Coins made from silver or any similar white metal."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made from silver.","Made from another white metal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silver"},{"term":"sweetpea","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of sweet pea."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweetpea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sweet pea","blocks":[{"text":"The sweet pea, Lathyrus odoratus, is a flowering plant in the genus Lathyrus in the family Fabaceae (legumes), native to Sicily, southern Italy and the Aegean Islands."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Sweet_Pea-7.jpg/330px-Sweet_Pea-7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweet_pea","wikidata":"Q163944"},{"title":"Silver","blocks":[{"text":"Silver is a chemical element; it has symbol Ag and atomic number 47. A soft, white, lustrous transition metal, it exhibits the highest electrical conductivity, thermal conductivity and reflectivity of any metal. Silver is found in the Earth's crust in the pure, free elemental form, as an alloy with gold (electrum) and other metals, and in minerals such as acanthite, argentite and chlorargyrite. Most silver is recovered as a byproduct of lead–zinc, copper and gold mining and refining."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Silver_crystal.jpg/330px-Silver_crystal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver","wikidata":"Q1090"},{"title":"Silver (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Silver or metallic gray is a color tone resembling gray that is a representation of the color of polished silver."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Clemens_Friedell_silver_centerpiece_bowl_top_view_-_HLABG.png/330px-Clemens_Friedell_silver_centerpiece_bowl_top_view_-_HLABG.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_(color)","wikidata":"Q317802"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Wm._Elliott_and_Sons%2C_seedsmen_%281897%29_%2814581816770%29.jpg/500px-Wm._Elliott_and_Sons%2C_seedsmen_%281897%29_%2814581816770%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Wm._Elliott_and_Sons%2C_seedsmen_%281897%29_%2814581816770%29.jpg/1280px-Wm._Elliott_and_Sons%2C_seedsmen_%281897%29_%2814581816770%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Wm._Elliott_and_Sons%2C_seedsmen_%281897%29_%2814581816770%29.jpg/500px-Wm._Elliott_and_Sons%2C_seedsmen_%281897%29_%2814581816770%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sweet peas, advertised 1897","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWm._Elliott_and_Sons%2C_seedsmen_(1897)_(14581816770).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Sweet_pea_%28Lathyrus_odoratus%29_seeds.jpg/500px-Sweet_pea_%28Lathyrus_odoratus%29_seeds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Sweet_pea_%28Lathyrus_odoratus%29_seeds.jpg/1280px-Sweet_pea_%28Lathyrus_odoratus%29_seeds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Sweet_pea_%28Lathyrus_odoratus%29_seeds.jpg/500px-Sweet_pea_%28Lathyrus_odoratus%29_seeds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conten